<<<
scarce, adv., used instead of scarcely, is a LITERARY WORD. It is true that the OED says: ‘ Before adverbs in -ly the form scarce is often adopted instead of scarcely, to avoid the iteration of the suffix ’.
===
**scarce,** adv., used instead of *scarcely*, is a ^^LITERARY WORD^^. It is true that the OED says: 'Before adverbs in *-ly* the form *scarce* is often adopted instead of *scarcely*, to avoid the iteration of the suffix'.
>>>

